dist.ini still shells out to docker build / docker push in four run_after_release lines. With DOCKER_HOST on the rootless Podman socket that build dies in buildx and takes the git release steps with it (happened on the Skeid 0.003 release). Replace the lines with docker_image = raudssus/langertha-knarr (Author::GETTY 0.326, Docker::API 0.104), keep the gh release lines, keep a way to pass LANGERTHA_SRC at release time (today KNARR_DOCKER_BUILD_ARGS). Same change as skeid k89; take over what was found there.

Orchestrator: Dockerfile has no ARG LANGERTHA_SRC since 3715f45 (Dockerfile rewrite), so KNARR_DOCKER_BUILD_ARGS/LANGERTHA_SRC is already a no-op in knarr. From skeid k89: Docker::API build_arg templates expand dist variables only, no env expansion; bundle auto-default passes no build_arg. Base change (docker_image + docker_tags = latest %V %v, gh lines kept) goes to knarr-worker; LANGERTHA_SRC question goes to the maintainer.

Maintainer decision: drop LANGERTHA_SRC / KNARR_DOCKER_BUILD_ARGS without replacement (no ARG in the Dockerfile, no build_arg subsection).

